/*!
    \class vsmm::IHttpClient
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief Interface for asynchronous HTTP GET requests with callbacks.

    IHttpClient declares one operation, sendGet(). The caller passes the URL,
    a context object, the expected content type and three callbacks. The
    implementation calls the success callback with the response body, or the
    failure callback with an error message. A progress callback receives
    download progress.

    \l vsmm::HttpClient is the implementation the application uses. Tests use
    a mock of this interface. \l vsmm::ModLoader uses it to fetch mod info from
    the mod API and to download mod updates. \l vsmm::ModImageProvider uses it
    to download mod icons.

    \sa vsmm::HttpClient
*/

/*!
    \typedef vsmm::IHttpClient::SuccessFn

    Callback type \c {std::function<void(QByteArray)>}. It receives the body
    of a successful response.
*/

/*!
    \typedef vsmm::IHttpClient::FailedFn

    Callback type \c {std::function<void(QString)>}. It receives a message
    that describes why the request failed.
*/

/*!
    \typedef vsmm::IHttpClient::ProgressFn

    Callback type \c {std::function<void(qint64 received, qint64 total)>}.
    It receives the number of bytes received so far and the total number of
    bytes of the response. \a total is \c -1 when the size is unknown.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::IHttpClient::~IHttpClient()

    Destroys the interface.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IHttpClient::sendGet(const QUrl &url, QObject *context, const QString &contentType, vsmm::IHttpClient::SuccessFn successFn, vsmm::IHttpClient::FailedFn failedFn, vsmm::IHttpClient::ProgressFn progressFn)

    Sends a GET request to \a url and returns without waiting for the
    response.

    When the response arrives and its content type starts with
    \a contentType, the implementation calls \a successFn with the response
    body. On failure it calls \a failedFn with an error message.
    \a progressFn receives download progress while the response arrives.
    The callbacks are bound to \a context.

    \sa vsmm::HttpClient::sendGet()
*/

/*!
    \class vsmm::HttpClient
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief HTTP client based on QNetworkAccessManager, with a disk cache and retries.

    HttpClient implements \l vsmm::IHttpClient. It owns a
    QNetworkAccessManager and a QNetworkDiskCache. The cache directory is
    QStandardPaths::CacheLocation and the cache size limit is 200 MiB.

    Every request sets the \c User-Agent header to the application name and
    version, separated by a slash, and uses a transfer timeout of 15 seconds.
    The first attempt uses QNetworkRequest::PreferNetwork. Retries use
    QNetworkRequest::AlwaysNetwork, so a retry never reads the cache.

    A failed request is retried up to three times. HTTP status 408, 429, 500,
    502, 503 and 504 are retried. Other 4xx status codes and 501 are not
    retried. Other network errors are retried. The delay before a retry is
    the value of the \c Retry-After header in seconds, when the header holds
    a non-negative integer. Otherwise the delay starts at 500 milliseconds
    and doubles with each retry. The delay is never longer than 10 seconds.

    A request fails when the reply has an error or the HTTP status is not
    200. The failure message contains the Qt error string and the HTTP
    status. A request also fails when the \c Content-Type header of the
    response does not start with the expected content type. The prefix check
    lets a caller pass \c {image/} to accept any image type. When all checks
    pass, the client reads the whole response body and passes it to the
    success callback.

    \sa vsmm::IHttpClient
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::HttpClient::HttpClient(QObject *parent)

    Constructs a client with the given \a parent and sets up its disk cache.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::HttpClient::~HttpClient()

    Destroys the client. A retry scheduled before the client is destroyed
    does not send a new request.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::HttpClient::sendGet(const QUrl &url, QObject *context, const QString &contentType, vsmm::IHttpClient::SuccessFn successFn, vsmm::IHttpClient::FailedFn failedFn, vsmm::IHttpClient::ProgressFn progressFn)
    \reimp

    Sends the request with the retry, cache and content type rules described
    in the class documentation. \a failedFn and \a progressFn can be empty,
    \a progressFn is only called while the HTTP status is 200, and no
    callback runs after \a context is destroyed.
*/

/*!
    \class vsmm::ZipArchive
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief Read-only access to the entries of a zip file, based on libzip.

    ZipArchive opens a zip file in read-only mode and reads single entries
    into memory. The constructor only stores the path. Call open() before
    reading. Look up an entry by name with getFileIndex(), then read its
    content with getFileContent().

    Every function that can fail returns a \c std::expected. The error is a
    message that names the archive and contains the libzip error, when there
    is one.

    \l vsmm::ModLoader uses ZipArchive to read \c modinfo.json from a mod zip
    file.

    The class can be moved but not copied. The destructor closes the archive
    when it is open.

    \code
    vsmm::ZipArchive archive(path);
    if (const auto opened = archive.open(); !opened) {
        return opened.error();
    }
    const auto index = archive.getFileIndex("modinfo.json");
    if (!index) {
        return index.error();
    }
    const auto content = archive.getFileContent(*index);
    \endcode
*/

/*!
    \typedef vsmm::ZipArchive::FileIndex

    Index of an entry in the archive. It is the libzip type \c zip_int64_t.

    \sa getFileIndex(), getFileContent()
*/

/*!
    \typedef vsmm::ZipArchive::FileContentSize

    Size of the content of an entry. It is the libzip type \c zip_int64_t.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::ZipArchive::ZipArchive(QString file)

    Constructs an archive for the zip file at the path \a file. The file is
    not opened until open() is called.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::ZipArchive::ZipArchive(vsmm::ZipArchive &&other) noexcept

    Move-constructs an archive from \a other. The new object takes the open
    archive of \a other, and \a other is left without an open archive.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::ZipArchive &vsmm::ZipArchive::operator=(vsmm::ZipArchive &&other) noexcept

    Move-assigns \a other to this archive and returns a reference to this
    archive. The two objects swap their paths and archive handles, so
    \a other closes the previous archive of this object when it is destroyed.
*/

/*!
    \fn std::expected<void, QString> vsmm::ZipArchive::open()

    Opens the zip file in read-only mode. Returns an empty value on success
    and when the archive is already open. Returns an error message when
    libzip cannot open the file.
*/

/*!
    \fn std::expected<vsmm::ZipArchive::FileIndex, QString> vsmm::ZipArchive::getFileIndex(QUtf8StringView fileName) const

    Returns the index of the entry named \a fileName. The name is UTF-8.

    Returns an error message when the archive is not open or when no entry
    has this name.

    \sa getFileContent()
*/

/*!
    \fn std::expected<QByteArray, QString> vsmm::ZipArchive::getFileContent(vsmm::ZipArchive::FileIndex fileIndex) const

    Reads the whole uncompressed content of the entry at \a fileIndex and
    returns it.

    Returns an error message when the archive is not open, when libzip
    cannot read the entry information, when the entry size is unknown, when
    the entry cannot be opened, or when fewer bytes than the entry size are
    read.

    \sa getFileIndex()
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::ZipArchive::~ZipArchive()

    Destroys the object and closes the archive when it is open.
*/
